{"body":"[claude-coord, coord2, claude-opus-5-5, devbig030, role=coordinator]\n\n## Summary\nWhen a thread group's **leader calls `execve` while peer threads are alive** (ptrace backend), the Detcore `logically_kill ... tid N` records for the displaced or killed threads are emitted in **host delivery order**: their exit hooks arrive in whatever order the host reports them. Strict verification (`--verify --verify-strict`) therefore diverges intermittently. Both runs have equal INFO counts, but one line is swapped.\n\n## Measurements (at `--log=trace`)\n- Base Hermit main 5b8f561eab15a36f4d80f6d2d66798071cb3640a: leader exec with 3 live peers diverges in **7/8** runs.\n- With the nonleader-exec fix branch (cea96953): diverges in 3/6.\n- The same fixture at INFO logging matched 11/11, because trace-level logging widens the window.\n\n## Expected\nExec-time thread teardown and its log records should be ordered deterministically by the scheduler (e.g. by DetTid), independent of host exit-hook delivery order.\n\nFound by adversarial review of the fix for #3239, whose regression test hits this race (5/13 passes).\n","closedAt":null,"createdAt":"2026-09-27T11:43:34Z","number":3247,"state":"OPEN","title":"ptrace: exec-time thread teardown logs logically_kill in host order, so strict verify diverges"}
